# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Meridian's own tests embed fixtures as raw string literals in .cs files and compare
# adapter output against them. With platform-native checkout those literals arrive as
# CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere, so the same assertion means two different things
# depending on who checked out the repo. Pinning the working tree makes the tests
# deterministic; git still detects binary content and leaves it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary fixtures.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.msapp binary
